          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "كهرباء — kahrabāʾ — \"electricity\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تعمل الثلاجة بالكهرباء. taʿmalu ath-thallāja bi-l-kahrabāʾ. The fridge runs on electricity."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "كهرباء (kahrabāʾ) goes back to Persian kahrubā, \"amber\" (EtymDB), a name usually read as \"straw-robber\", since rubbed amber draws straw to it; the old name passed to electricity."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
